From: Iscandar-ram build (Paper 3, Task 8 fix round)
Subject: [PATCH 0008] bridge core: confirm-then-commit raise, dead man's switch

Applies on top of 0007's core as it stands in the tree
(mm/iscandar_bridge.c, 551 lines). Implements the Task 8
fix round of build/bridge/TASK8-FIXROUND-DRAFT.md, as
ruled 2026-11-18 (no steps skipped; the failure
documented in BENCH-RUN-SHEET.md, bench findings of
2026-11-18 late evening: 32 registrations served, the
layer dead after serve 32, ready standing over a dead
channel, the system starved on NULL):

D1, the raise: a raise window (iscandar_raising) admits
registration calls while the doors, gated on ready,
stay shut. The first registration failure aborts the
enumeration and unrolls it locally; ready is written
only after the whole list has registered. A failed
raise leaves prefix posture untouched.

D2, layer death: three consecutive bridge timeouts
close the bridge (iscandar_closed): ready falls, the
doors serve stock, and later calls refuse at once
instead of stalling five seconds each. An arena free
that reaches a closed or timed-out bridge is leaked
and counted (the doors never hand an arena pointer to
the stock free); the count stands in the bridge read
beside the timeouts, and the state line reports
"closed". A later raise clears the closure and tries
again. The unregister's destroy crosses only while
ready stands; in a rollback or after closure it is
local only.

The shared header, the control block, the canary, and
the engine text are untouched. The unit-web half of
the round (D3) and the span-identity link check (D4)
live in the unit files, the ELBE XML, and
link-check.sh, not in this patch.

